# Enforcement-layer hooks. `core.autocrlf=true` on the founder's machine would
# otherwise hand these to bash with CRLF endings. Git Bash tolerates that today
# (measured: a CRLF-ified guard still passes the selftest 64/0), but a stray CR
# is a classic silent-failure source in shell -- and a hook that silently stops
# enforcing is exactly the failure this layer exists to end. Pin LF.
.claude/hooks/*.sh               text eol=lf
.claude/settings.json            text eol=lf

# CI: a workflow with CRLF line endings fails on the runner in ways that read as
# a script bug rather than a checkout bug.
.github/workflows/*.yml          text eol=lf
